{
  "info": {
    "name": "HEK — 4 APIs Manual Verification (New vs Real Legacy)",
    "description": "Every request in this collection uses REAL, hardcoded values (patient 2450776, encounter 19592581__901__FZZ999-B) already confirmed working on 2026-07-31 — nothing needs to be filled in. For each operation there are two requests, one under 'NEW API' and one under 'REAL LEGACY' with the exact same input — run both and compare the response body. The only things NOT hardcoded are the 3 login tokens ({{ermsToken}}, {{karoToken}}, {{colToken}}) — those are captured automatically the moment you run the 'Authenticate' request in each folder, so just run requests top to bottom within a folder.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. HISO (SOAP)",
      "description": "IMPORTANT — every HISO operation, including getVersion, requires a real sessionKey (a GUID). getVersion's response payload is otherwise hardcoded, but the session itself is still checked first — legacy rejects an empty/wrong sessionKey with 'Invalid Session Key'. The sessionKey below (439CC902-4C78-4F9A-A001-837C553DE0C1) is a REAL, currently-active session for practice 901 confirmed live on 2026-07-31 — HISO sessions in this system do not expire, so it should keep working, but if either side ever returns 'Invalid Session Key', ask engineering for a fresh one (query the HekTenantRegistry database's HisoSessions table for an IsActive=1 row, practice 901). ALSO IMPORTANT: the SOAPAction header must be exactly 'http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession/<operationName>' — real legacy strictly rejects any other form of this header (e.g. with '/IFormSessionService/' in it) with an ActionNotSupported fault, even though the new API is more lenient about it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "NEW API — getVersion",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [ { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/xml; charset=utf-8" }, { "key": "SOAPAction", "value": "\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession/getVersion\"" } ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=\"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/\" xmlns:tns=\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession\">\n  <soap:Body>\n    <tns:getVersion><tns:sessionKey>439CC902-4C78-4F9A-A001-837C553DE0C1</tns:sessionKey></tns:getVersion>\n  </soap:Body>\n</soap:Envelope>" },
            "url": "http://localhost:8080/FormSessionService.svc"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "REAL LEGACY — getVersion",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [ { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/xml; charset=utf-8" }, { "key": "SOAPAction", "value": "\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession/getVersion\"" } ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=\"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/\" xmlns:tns=\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession\">\n  <soap:Body>\n    <tns:getVersion><tns:sessionKey>439CC902-4C78-4F9A-A001-837C553DE0C1</tns:sessionKey></tns:getVersion>\n  </soap:Body>\n</soap:Envelope>" },
            "url": "http://localhost:53507/FormSessionService.svc"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "NEW API — getDeliveryOptions",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [ { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/xml; charset=utf-8" }, { "key": "SOAPAction", "value": "\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession/getDeliveryOptions\"" } ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=\"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/\" xmlns:tns=\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession\">\n  <soap:Body>\n    <tns:getDeliveryOptions><tns:sessionKey>439CC902-4C78-4F9A-A001-837C553DE0C1</tns:sessionKey></tns:getDeliveryOptions>\n  </soap:Body>\n</soap:Envelope>" },
            "url": "http://localhost:8080/FormSessionService.svc"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "REAL LEGACY — getDeliveryOptions (NOTE: senderPassword/URL are placeholder CHANGE_ME on the new API — real HealthLink credentials never supplied, known/documented gap)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [ { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/xml; charset=utf-8" }, { "key": "SOAPAction", "value": "\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession/getDeliveryOptions\"" } ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=\"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/\" xmlns:tns=\"http://www.hiso.govt.nz/10014.2/1.0/formsession\">\n  <soap:Body>\n    <tns:getDeliveryOptions><tns:sessionKey>439CC902-4C78-4F9A-A001-837C553DE0C1</tns:sessionKey></tns:getDeliveryOptions>\n  </soap:Body>\n</soap:Envelope>" },
            "url": "http://localhost:53507/FormSessionService.svc"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "NOTE — getData / saveContainer / getFormView / processAction",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8080/README-these-4-need-a-live-form-instance"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": { "exec": [ "// These 4 HISO operations need a sessionKey the same way getVersion/getDeliveryOptions do, PLUS a real formInstanceId/ACC45 record tied to that exact session.", "// The reusable session above (439CC902-...) currently has no ACC45 form data attached to it (confirmed live 2026-07-31), so it cannot be used for these 4 on its own.", "// To test these 4 operations: ask engineering for a session + formInstanceId pair that is currently populated with real data, captured at the time you want to test.", "// This request intentionally does nothing — it is a placeholder note only." ], "type": "text/javascript" }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
